{"step_index":1676,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-19T19:48:09Z","input_tokens":4075,"cache_read_tokens":207450,"output_tokens":2325,"thinking":"The Bybit testnet environment initializes with a starting balance of 15.00. An `activePosition` state variable is managed, initially set to null, likely representing the current open trading position. The system utilizes a `useEffect` hook that responds to real-time updates from a Bybit WebSocket feed to handle tick evaluation.\n\n\nCalculating unrealized profit/loss based on the current price from the Bybit feed relative to the entry price of the active position, accounting for trade direction and fees. The system checks if take-profit or stop-loss levels are hit, determining the final profit or loss amount. Finally, the balance updates and the peak balance is checked.\n\n\nUpdating the balance, incrementing trades copied, and resetting loss streaks are necessary actions following a trade's outcome.  Experience and weight adaptation occur based on whether the trade resulted in a win or loss, influencing future decision-making parameters.\n\nRecording the trade details—including profit/loss, instrument, and time—in the logs and updating the chart history provides a comprehensive audit trail for performance analysis and visualization.\n\n\nPosition closure logic triggers when take-profit or stop-loss levels are reached, updating the displayed thought and clearing the active position.  The active position's current price and unrealized profit/loss are updated continuously when open, ensuring the current state is tracked.\n\nA new position opens when no position is currently active, and the simulation is running, using a recent market imbalance for a strong signal. The logic checks for a strong market imbalance and a lack of news lock before deciding to initiate a buy or sell order. Position size is a fixed BTC amount, with calculated notional value and margin usage based on the current BTC price.\n\n\nA new position is initialized only if one isn't already open, and specific market conditions are met.  Stop-loss, take-profit, and liquidation prices are calculated based on entry price and trade direction (buy/sell). Details of the new position, including entry price, stop-loss, take-profit, and margin are logged and the active position state updated. The balance is modified.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"view_file","args":{"AbsolutePath":"\"/Users/dev/Documents/Antigravity/grok-bot-dashboard/src/engine/useTradingSimulation.ts\"","EndLine":"70","StartLine":"30","toolAction":"\"Checking starting balance constant\"","toolSummary":"\"Check starting balance constant\""}}]}
